.Dd August 1, 2026
.Dt INTEGRIS-CRASH-STUB 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm integris-crash-stub
.Nd Integris engineering crash harness for publish and journal labels
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a Unix-only engineering helper that exercises crash points in publication
or journal append paths by requesting an OS
.Dv SIGKILL
at a labeled persistence step (IP-S-0003 catalog).
It supports recovery and fault-injection campaigns.
.Pp
It is not a product daemon and must not be confused with
.Xr integrisd 8 .
.Pp
The process refuses to start unless
.Ev INTEGRIS_LAUNCH_MODE
is
.Li engineering .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "INTEGRIS_CRASH_FAIL_AT"
.It Ev INTEGRIS_LAUNCH_MODE
Must be
.Li engineering .
.It Ev INTEGRIS_CRASH_ROOT
Required working directory for the harness.
.It Ev INTEGRIS_CRASH_FAIL_AT
Required KillAt / FailAt label from the IP-S-0003 catalog
(for example publication stage/rename/dirsync labels or journal append labels).
.It Ev INTEGRIS_CRASH_MODE
.Li publish
(default) or
.Li journal .
.It Ev INTEGRIS_CRASH_NAME
Required object name when mode is
.Li publish .
.It Ev INTEGRIS_CRASH_DATA
Optional payload for publish mode.
Default:
.Li crash-stub-payload .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Harness completed without error (uncommon when a kill label fires).
.It 1
Invalid environment, I/O failure, or non-engineering launch mode.
.El
.Pp
When a kill label is hit, the process is terminated by
.Dv SIGKILL
and may not return an exit status to the parent.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Invoked by recovery tests / launcher; not a user-facing CLI.
# INTEGRIS_LAUNCH_MODE=engineering \\
#   INTEGRIS_CRASH_ROOT=/tmp/crash \\
#   INTEGRIS_CRASH_FAIL_AT=P-PUBLISH-RENAME \\
#   INTEGRIS_CRASH_NAME=obj integris-crash-stub
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr integris-evidence 1 ,
.Xr integris-role-stub 1 ,
.Xr kill 1 ,
.Xr integris 7 ,
.Xr integrisd 8
.Pp
.Pa docs/ip/IP-S-0003-idempotent-crash-recovery.md
.Sh HISTORY
Introduced to provide an OS-level SIGKILL harness for recovery evidence.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Integris contributors
.Sh CAVEATS
Available only on Unix builds (//go:build unix).
Not included in all CI distribution artifact lists; built on demand by the
launcher and tests.
Do not install as a system service.
See
.Pa TRADEMARKS.md .
